de prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 7 grids runs from 1951 to 2025, and September to October came in under 90% of normal in 39 of those 75 years, more than any other pair. In 2025 the middle of the grids got 162% of normal in April to May and just 43% in October to November. For 2026 so far, March to April came in at 37% of normal on the middle of the grids. Grid 21510 had its driest year in 1963 at 68% of normal.</p>"}
